# Packages installed into the live image.
#
# Derived from archiso's `releng` list, with three deliberate changes:
#
#  1. ADDED the desktop: `nidara` (from the [nidara] repo — see pacman.conf) and
#     the handful of things a live desktop needs that a rescue shell does not.
#     `nidara` pulls Hyprland, GTK4/GJS, PipeWire, portals, fonts and its own
#     default apps through its depends=() — none of that is listed here.
#  2. SWAPPED the network stack: releng boots iwd + systemd-networkd; Nidara's
#     shell reads NetworkManager's libnm directly, so the live session has to be
#     on NetworkManager or its network panel is blind. This is not a preference.
#  3. REMOVED the rescue-DVD toolbox (clonezilla, partclone, partimage, ddrescue,
#     testdisk, fsarchiver, dmraid, jfsutils, nilfs-utils…), the terminal
#     userland nobody reaches from a desktop (irssi, lynx, mc, screen, tmux,
#     lftp, nmap…) and the VPN/dial-up clients (openvpn, vpnc, openconnect, ppp,
#     pptpclient, xl2tpd, wvdial — NetworkManager plugins cover the modern half).
#     This is an install medium for a desktop, not a maintenance DVD, and every
#     megabyte here is a megabyte of download.
#
# Hardware support is NOT part of that trim: firmware, filesystem tools, wifi
# drivers and VM guest agents stay exactly as releng has them.

# ── base system ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
base
linux
linux-firmware
linux-firmware-marvell
amd-ucode
intel-ucode
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
sof-firmware
sudo
less
nano
man-db
man-pages
terminus-font

# ── the desktop ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The only two packages on this list that do not come from Arch's own repos.
#
# They answer two different questions, which is why they are two packages and
# not one. `nidara` is what the desktop needs to RUN — without it there is no
# shell. `nidara-apps` is what makes a freshly installed machine USABLE: a
# browser, and whatever else that set turns out to be. Its contents are
# deliberately undecided and live in nidara-repo, one line away from changing;
# what matters here is that the ISO names both and `install.sh` names only the
# first (it runs on an Arch someone already uses, with their own apps chosen).
#
# Everything BELOW this section is the medium's own: kernel, firmware, installer
# tools, VM guest agents. None of it belongs on the machine this ISO installs —
# that system gets `nidara` + `nidara-apps` and nothing else from here. Keeping
# the two apart is why the browser is no longer a line in this file.
nidara
nidara-apps

# ── installing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
arch-install-scripts
archinstall
btrfs-progs
cryptsetup
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
efibootmgr
exfatprogs
f2fs-tools
gptfdisk
grub
lvm2
mdadm
mtools
nvme-cli
ntfsprogs
parted
reflector
squashfs-tools
syslinux
xfsprogs

# ── network ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
networkmanager
modemmanager
usb_modeswitch
wpa_supplicant
wireless-regdb
wireless_tools
iw
b43-fwcutter
broadcom-wl
openssh
rsync
bind
systemd-resolvconf

# ── hardware / storage ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bolt
dmidecode
ethtool
hdparm
libfido2
libusb-compat
lsscsi
mmc-utils
pcsclite
sdparm
sg3_utils
smartmontools
tpm2-tools
tpm2-tss
usbutils
usbmuxd
alsa-utils

# ── virtual machines (this image is tested in one) ───────────────────────────
qemu-guest-agent
open-vm-tools
virtualbox-guest-utils-nox
hyperv
